Since a single label of disease given out as a diagnosis can be very misleading and cause a huge rate of misdiagnosis, there should be multiple diseases
showcased to the patient with the probability of them occuring.

The probability will be paired with their respective encoded disease, the top 5 pairs will be extracted and the encoded diseases
will be decoded back into their original string form. 

Then the patient will see an output that looks something like this:

Malaria : 70%
AIDS : 20%
Other diseases : 10%


To pair the encoded disease with their respective probability,

classifier.classes_ : Encoded diseases(0-40)
diagnosis = Probability

The diagnosis is a 2D array therefore the flat 1D array should be extracted first and then only will the probabilities be extracted.

Not only do the classifiers predict probabilities for all 41 diseases but also position them in the same order as their respective 
encoded diseases. 

dancing = [ ]
for name_of_classifier,classifier in classifier_dictionary.items():
  diagnosis = classifier.predict_proba(itum_bahal)
  disease_class = classifier.classes_
  flattened_diagnosis = diagnosis[0]
  for position in range(0,41):
    dancing.append((int(disease_class[position]),float(flattened_diagnosis[position])))
print(dancing)

